#   1. The request tree is seeded from the fetched base, so a request changes
#      ONLY its target paths. Unseeded, it proposes deleting the whole blueprint.
#   2. The commit is byte-reproducible, which is what lets a retry recognise its
#      own earlier request instead of refusing forever.
